From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 07:06:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] chore(release): regenerate D20 bd-audit artifact for shifted
 line numbers

This PR's bin/forge.js edits (per-command --help, bare-forge, setup-help) and
lib/commands/status.js edits (one-glance view) added lines, shifting the exact
bd/.beads reference line numbers the D20 kill-list artifact records. The audit
records line numbers per file, so the real `forge release check` gate flagged
the artifact stale even though ZERO bd/.beads/dolt tokens were added.

Deterministic snapshot refresh via renderBdCallSiteAuditMarkdown(auditBdCallSites):
only the bin/forge.js and lib/commands/status.js line-number lists move; counts
are unchanged (26 and 10). `forge release check --target 0.1.0` now passes with 0
blockers and test/commands/release.test.js is green. Authorized by team-lead
(line-shift is caused by this PR's owned-file edits, so the regen is in-scope).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
